1. e4 g6 2. d4 Bg7 3. Nc3 d6 4. Nf3 c6 5. h3 Nf6 6. Be2 O-O 7. Bf4 b5 8. a3 a6
9. O-O Nbd7 10. e5 Ne8 11. Re1 Nb6 12. Bf1 f6 13. Qd2 d5 14. a4 Nc7 15. b3 b4
16. Nd1 a5 17. Nb2 Ne6 18. exf6 exf6 19. Nd3 Nxf4 20. Qxf4 g5 21. Qg3 Rf7 22.
Re2 Bf8 23. Rae1 Bf5 24. Nc5 Qd6 25. Qxd6 Bxd6 26. g4 Bd7 27. Nxd7 Rxd7 28. Re6
Kf7 29. Bd3 h6 30. Bf5 Rad8 31. h4 Nc8 32. h5 Ne7 33. Bd3 (33. Ne5+ $1) 33...
Rf8 34. Kg2 Ke8 35. Nd2 Kd8 36. Nf1 Kc7 37. Ng3 Bf4 38. Rxe7 {By preventing
Black from playing ....e5 and ....b4 White maintains an advantage in space
which gives him chance to choose his moment to open up the position.33Ne5+!
wins. The e file is what cost Black the game.37....Bf4 blunders a piece but
Black was losing anyway.} 1-0

